      "text": "# Transactional Inventory Ledger: Design & Reference Implementation\n\n## 1. Design Overview\n\nThis system implements an **append-only, double-entry-style inventory ledger** in SQLite with:\n- **Idempotent transactions** via client-generated UUIDs\n- **Optimistic concurrency control** with versioned stock levels\n- **Audit invariants** enforced at the database level\n- **Safe migrations** with rollback support\n- **Full test coverage**\n\n### Core Principles\n1. **Immutability**: Stock movements are never updated/deleted; corrections are new entries.\n2. **Idempotency**: Re-submitting the same transaction ID is a no-op.\n3. **Consistency**: Stock levels are derived from the ledger, never stored as mutable truth.\n4. **Auditability**: Every change is traceable to a transaction with timestamp, actor, and reason.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Schema Design\n\n```sql\n-- ============================================================\n-- INVENTORY LEDGER SCHEMA\n-- ============================================================\n\n-- Products: static catalog (not part of ledger)\nCREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS products (\n    product_id   TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\n    name         TEXT NOT NULL,\n    sku          TEXT UNIQUE NOT NULL,\n    created_at   TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT (strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%fZ', 'now')),\n    updated_at   TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT (strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%fZ', 'now'))\n);\n\n-- Stock movements: the immutable ledger\n-- Each row represents a single atomic change to inventory\nCREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS stock_movements (\n    movement_id      INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT,\n    transaction_id   TEXT NOT NULL UNIQUE,          -- Idempotency key (client-generated UUID)\n    product_id       TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES products(product_id),\n    quantity_change  INTEGER NOT NULL,              -- Positive = inbound, Negative = outbound\n    balance_after    INTEGER NOT NULL,              -- Derived: stock level after this movement\n    movement_type    TEXT NOT NULL CHECK (movement_type IN (\n                         'INBOUND', 'OUTBOUND', 'ADJUSTMENT', 'TRANSFER_IN', 'TRANSFER_OUT'\n                     )),\n    reason           TEXT NOT NULL,                 -- Human-readable reason\n    actor            TEXT NOT NULL,                 -- User/system that initiated\n    occurred_at      TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT (strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%fZ', 'now')),\n    created_at       TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT (strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%fZ', 'now')),\n    version          INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 1,    -- Optimistic lock version for concurrency\n    FOREIGN KEY (product_id) REFERENCES products(product_id)\n);\n\n-- Indexes for performance\nCREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_movements_product ON stock_movements(product_id);\nCREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_movements_transaction ON stock_movements(transaction_id);\nCREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_movements_occurred ON stock_movements(occurred_at);\nCREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_movements_product_occurred ON stock_movements(product_id, occurred_at);\n\n-- Materialized view: current stock levels (derived, not source of truth)\n-- This is a convenience table, rebuilt from ledger on demand\nCREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS stock_levels (\n    product_id   TEXT PRIMARY KEY REFERENCES products(product_id),\n    quantity     INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,\n    last_updated TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT (strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%fZ', 'now')),\n    version      INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 1\n);\n\n-- Audit log: tracks schema/data changes for compliance\nCREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS audit_log (\n    audit_id     INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT,\n    action       TEXT NOT NULL,                     -- 'INSERT', 'UPDATE', 'DELETE', 'MIGRATION'\n    table_name   TEXT NOT NULL,\n    record_id    TEXT,\n    old_values   TEXT,                              -- JSON\n    new_values   TEXT,                              -- JSON\n    actor        TEXT NOT NULL,\n    occurred_at  TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT (strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%fZ', 'now'))\n);\n\n-- Migration tracking\nCREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS schema_migrations (\n    version      INTEGER PRIMARY KEY,\n    name         TEXT NOT NULL,\n    applied_at   TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT (strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%fZ', 'now')),\n    checksum     TEXT NOT NULL                      -- SHA256 of migration SQL\n);\n```\n\n### Key Design Decisions\n\n| Decision | Rationale |\n|----------|-----------|\n| `transaction_id` UNIQUE | Guarantees idempotency at DB level |\n| `balance_after` stored | Enables fast reads without summing all movements; validated on write",
